Couple explanations I can think of, barring a bones level...

Most likely it was a Chameleon.  You might've seen them before,
a monster that keeps changing into another monster and sometimes
leaves a corpse, a chameleon corpse.  Chameleons have a chance
to become just about any kind of monster, Arch-Liches included. 
The best strategy if you think it is a chameleon causing the
problem, try and avoid it for 20-30 turns, though this will be
tough with a teleporting Lich.  Engrave Elbereth and hope for
the best or simply avoid the level. 

Another possibility, a Gnome or something quaffed a potion of
polymorph that they were carrying or found somewhere.  This
scenario would be tougher to deal with, since the Gnome or
goblin or whoever quaffed the potion is now permenantly an
Arch-Lich... you'll definately have to avoid the level until you
can deal with it... Your cloak of magic resistance, Magicbane
and cold resistance could be enough to overpower a Lich if you
keep it from escaping and watch your HP. 

